\section*{Unified Action Formalism Across All USC-QSE Domains}
\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{Unified Action Formalism}

The USC-QSE-v5.2 engine expresses all physics subsystems through a unified
action principle. Each subsystem contributes a term to the total action:

\[
S_{\text{total}}
=
S_{\text{string}}
+
S_{\text{DM}}
+
S_{\text{QH}}
+
S_{\text{multi}}
+
S_{\text{grav}}.
\]

%==================================================
% STRING ACTION
%==================================================

\subsection*{String-Theoretic Action}

\[
S_{\text{string}}
=
-\frac{1}{4\pi\alpha'}
\int d^2\sigma \sqrt{-h}\,
h^{ab}
\partial_a X^\mu
\partial_b X_\mu.
\]

Conformal invariance:
\[
T^a_{\ a} = 0.
\]

Beta function constraint:
\[
\beta_{\mu\nu}
=
\alpha' R_{\mu\nu}
+
2\alpha' \nabla_\mu \nabla_\nu \Phi
=
0.
\]

This yields:
\[
R_{\mu\nu}
=
-2\nabla_\mu \nabla_\nu \Phi.
\]

