\subsection*{White-Hole Quantum Horizon Action}

The white-hole subsystem is governed by a quantum-corrected Einstein-Hilbert action:

\[
S_{\text{QH}}
=
\frac{c^3}{16\pi G}
\int d^4x \sqrt{-g}\,
\left[
R
+
\epsilon\,\mathcal{Q}(r,t)
\right].
\]

Quantum anomaly:
\[
\mathcal{Q}(r,t)
=
\beta\,\frac{\hbar}{r^3}.
\]

Metric:
\[
ds^2
=
-f(r,t)\,dt^2
+
f^{-1}(r,t)\,dr^2
+
r^2 d\Omega^2.
\]

Lapse:
\[
f(r,t)
=
1
-
\frac{2GM(r,t)}{r}
+
\epsilon\,\mathcal{Q}(r,t).
\]

Expansion scalar:
\[
\theta_+
=
\nabla_\mu k^\mu.
\]

Raychaudhuri equation:
\[
\frac{d\theta_+}{d\lambda}
=
-\frac{1}{2}\theta_+^2
-
\sigma_{\mu\nu}\sigma^{\mu\nu}
+
\omega_{\mu\nu}\omega^{\mu\nu}
-
R_{\mu\nu}k^\mu k^\nu.
\]

Anti-trapped condition:
\[
R_{\mu\nu}k^\mu k^\nu < 0
\Rightarrow
\theta_+ > 0.
\]

Blueshift:
\[
\nu_{\text{obs}}
=
\nu_{\text{emit}}
\sqrt{
\frac{f(r_{\text{emit}},t)}{f(\infty,t)}
}.
\]

